    },
    {
      "teacher_id": "A13",
      "node_type": "A",
      "label": "ResumeRank makes consequential employment decisions (auto-reject below 70), qualifying as high-risk AI under CO AIA 6-1-1701(7). However, applicability depends on whether Greenleaf operates in Colorado, which is plausible for a national chain but unconfirmed. If confirmed, both developer and deployer obligations apply.",
      "weight": 2.5
    },
    {
      "teacher_id": "A14",
      "node_type": "A",
      "label": "Greenleaf has 12,000 employees, far exceeding the 50-employee threshold in 6-1-1703(6)(a). The small deployer exception does not apply. All deployer obligations under 6-1-1703(2) would be required if CO AIA applies.",
      "weight": 2.5
    },
    {
      "teacher_id": "A15",
      "node_type": "A",
      "label": "If Greenleaf operates in CO, it currently lacks: NIST AI RMF-aligned risk management program, impact assessments, website statement, consumer notice mechanisms, data correction processes, and appeal mechanisms. All would be required by June 30, 2026 (or within 90 days for impact assessments of pre-existing deployments). Significant readiness gap exists.",
